cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "spTRACE: agent-based simulation of spatial transcriptomics data with allele-specific copy-number variation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jintong
    family-names: Shi
    email: jintongs@kth.se
    affiliation: "KTH Royal Institute of Technology"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jintong-shi/spTRACE"
abstract: >-
  An agent-based simulator that grows a tumour cell population on a 2-D lattice,
  mutating each cell's diploid genome with allele-specific copy-number events drawn
  from a real CNV catalogue, and infusing normal tumour-microenvironment cells during
  growth according to cell-type-specific spatial weight maps. The resulting tissue is
  rendered as single-cell expression, spot-level spatial transcriptomics, and allele
  (AD/DP) count matrices, with complete ground truth for benchmarking spatial
  copy-number inference methods.
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - copy number variation
  - simulation
  - benchmarking
  - tumour heterogeneity
  - single-cell